<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91889" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πύρφορ-ος</span></b>  (parox.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fire-bearing</i>,
			esp. of lightning, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. κεραυνός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					10.71
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				444
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1658
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστραπαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>OT</u>
					200
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διὸς ἔγχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					1749
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρφόρος αἰθέρος ἀστήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					1050
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. οἰστοί</span> arrows <i>with
				combustibles tied to them</i>, so that they may set fire to
			woodwork, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.75
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>An.</u>
				2.21.3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς μὲν π . . . τοῖς δ᾽ ἄλλοις βέλεσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					20.96
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ π</span>. ibid.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρφόρα, τά</span>,
			ib. <i><span class="en">
				88
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρφόρος, ὁ</span>, <i>engine for throwing fire, fire-dart</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				21.7.1
			</span></i> (dub.), <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				2.62d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in special
			senses, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> epith. of
			several divinities, as of Zeus in reference to his
			<i>lightnings</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1198
			</span></i> (anap.); of Demeter, prob. in reference to the
			<i>torches</i> used by her worshippers, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				260
			</span></i>; similarly <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. θεαί</span> of
			Demeter and Persephone, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				4.666.9
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Lerna</span>), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				687
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. Ἀρτέμιδος αἴγλας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					206
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Προμηθεὺς π</span>. the
				<i>Fire-bringer</i>, title of a satyric play of <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				55
			</span></i>; also of Capaneus, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				432
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				135
			</span></i> (lyr.); of Eros, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.87
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Rufin.
			</span></i>); but, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεὸς π</span>. <i>the
				fire-bearing</i> god, the god <i>who produces plague</i> or
				<i>fever</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				27
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>bearer of sacred fire</i> in the worship of Asclepius, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσκληπιοῦ δμῶα π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.693
			</span></i>; of the Syrian Goddess, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Syr.D.</u>
				42
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρφόρος, ὁ</span>, in the Spartan army, <i>the priest who kept
				the sacrificial fire</i>, which was never allowed to go out,
				<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Lac.</u>
				13.2
			</span></i>: hence prov. of a total defeat, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔδει δὲ μηδὲ πυρφόρον . . περιγενέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.6
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				39.45
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἔσται π</span>. (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυροφόρος</span>
			)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> τῷ οἴκῳ Ἠσαύ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ob.</u>
					18
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἡ ἐκ Δελφῶν</span>
			<i>bearer of sacred fire</i> from Delphi, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				711
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>D</u>
				22
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				728
			</span></i>
            <u>I</u>
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φοίβου πυρφόροι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					4.666.15
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Lerna</span>); also in a Bacchic thiasos, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AJA</u>
				37.253
			</span></i> (Latium, <span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>).</div>
